  "summary": [
    "Batch A, family A21 (complete and anticomplete pairs of supplied vertex sets), initially on the fixed A20 pin 229f295; combined on reviewed B23 parent 172629c. Three contracts stay apart: raw anticompleteness is upstream ~~ neighbor A B; the new GTBase.set_pairs names the disjoint anticomplete pair anticomplete A B ([disjoint A & B] && ~~ neighbor A B) and the cross-complete pair complete_between A B. Views: neighborNP, anticompleteP, anticomplete_nonadjP, complete_betweenP and disjoint_complete_betweenP, the last proving D2ram's explicit disjointness from cross completeness (complete_between_disjoint); swaps, restrictions and the complement duality for disjoint parts. The public client: empty parts and K_0, a shared K_1 singleton (raw anticomplete, neither disjoint-anticomplete nor complete), singleton parts of K_2 and of an edgeless graph, swaps and restrictions, a complete pair with a nonclique part in K_1,2, and the complement duality with its disjointness requirement.",
    "",
    "Frozen verbatim at 229f295: the ten sources, the five row-reaching chains (X57 sparse strong Erdos-Hajnal property; X41 and X144 pure pairs; X11 pairwise anticomplete paths and k paths) and the nine rows (Chromatic X3 #1111 and X213 El-Zahar-Erdos; Extremal X57, X58, X223 and D2ram; GTMisc X41 and X144; Minor X11). Complete rows at the pre-migration 9e03072: X57 (A1, with its property chain), X58 (A1), X41 (A1) and X11 (B1+B5, with both chains and B5's complete right alternative): 13 initial whole-row iffs; the bridges reuse A1's, B1's and B5's certificates. Quantifier orders, positivity guards, thresholds, asymmetric bounds, X223's closed-neighbourhood predicate, D2ram's G OR compl G branches, X41's documented sublinear side, statuses and leg states are unchanged.",
    "",
    "History: A1's X57/X58/X41 rows and B1's/B5's X11 chains keep live set-pair names byte for byte and are documented below, as is B5's X11Original, which reaches the live pair only through B1's frozen pairwise chain; A21's per-row copies keep A1's, B1's and B5's live names, with reciprocal notes in their specs. The two obsolete A8 exclusions of x223_anticomplete are removed; X76/X78 stay. Proof clients: grounding_X213, grounding_D2ram (both lemmas) and grounding_X223 route their raw conjunctions through the views with unchanged types; the verified gc:e076 implication X58 -> X223 is unchanged. The appended C12+A21 D2ram/X144 Originals freeze both raw perfection contracts and the complete raw pair chains. There are 41 frozen objects and 15 whole-row iffs (nine current, six Originals); the two new proofs require separate independent and coordinator review before acceptance."
  ],
